[Guid "Rcfe37c987fc040fdb64d144aa897768f"]
[ContentType "Intro"]
[White "Chapter"]
[Black "Introduction"]
[Result "*"]

{This Workbook is meant as a companion to Nigel Short's book "Winning" by Quality Chess 2021.   It contains all the games from that work so the reader can conveniently view them on the computer while reading the book.  The games have been imported from ChessBase's database and some of them come with comments by Short himself or by other GMs.  We have left those comments in as it may be interesting to compare them with what Short wrote in his book.  The Study view in each chapter has an 8-move opening variation tree combined from the games in the chapter. As always, you can press F3 to see the games in which the currently selected position can be found.  The games have been evaluated within Chess Forge with Stockfish 17. You will encounter annotation like this [? best: 17.♘f7] throughout. These are the result of the automatic error detection being turned on during the evaluation rather than commenters' notes.   In a few places we have added clarifying notes. Such notes are prefixed with CHF Note. }

