 {I have to make a shameful confession . I once made the mistake of addressing Joel by his widely used nickname. I apologise here and now for my rudeness. The Gods on Mount Olympus were clearly displeased and I was punished severely in our next game . That was only fair enough, I suppose. This was a tough game for me as I had been practically unemployed for several months, not having pushed pawns since the Goodricke tournament in Calcutta . I wish I could claim that I had used the time productively to repair and reinvigourate my battered opening repertoire but I had not. Apathy and sloth had characterised my mood at the time and by now there were barnacles on my play, or so it seemed.} 
