Nc6 {[%eval +0.30][%brsp d4]First of all I would like to point the attention of the readers of these lines to the fact that only for the 3rd time in his history Boris Gelfand goes for Sveshnikov Variation of the Sicilian Defence. His main weapon is Najdorf with more than 110 games played. Personally I think the choice of the Sveshnikov was a mistake, which contributed much to the Boris's loss of the present game. Without much experience in the variation you should not try something new against a very strong player such as Nigel Short.}  
